BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:5f8de4eef51f5300@kidcal
DTSTAMP:20260819T001543Z
DTSTART:20260924T220000Z
DTEND:20260924T230000Z
SUMMARY:Walking the White Blazes: Exploring the Appalachian Trail
LOCATION:Ruth Huntress Auditorium
URL:https://keenenh.libcal.com/event/17178782
CATEGORIES:kids\,Keene Public Library
DESCRIPTION:Stretching over 2\,190 miles from Georgia to Maine\, the Appal
 achian Trail is one of the world's most famous footpath journeys. Join us 
 for an engaging presentation that traces the history\, landscapes\, and cu
 lture of "the A.T."\n\nWe’ll explore the rich origins of the trail\, jou
 rney through the 14 states it traverses\, and highlight the diverse flora 
 and fauna—from mountain laurels to black bears—that hikers encounter a
 long the way. You’ll also learn unique trail lingo like thru-hiking\, tr
 ail magic\, and zero days. Whether you're an experienced backpacker\, a ca
 sual day-hiker\, or an armchair traveler\, you'll leave with a deeper appr
 eciation for this iconic American treasure.\n\nPresented by Jay Fee\, who 
 hiked the Appalachian Trail in 2000\, and is now Library Systems Administr
 ator for the Keene Public Library.\nSource: Keene Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:4f88c06e38ae7451@kidcal
DTSTAMP:20260819T001543Z
DTSTART:20260928T200000Z
DTEND:20260928T210000Z
SUMMARY:Library Build a Rama
LOCATION:Youth Department
URL:https://keenenh.libcal.com/event/17103893
CATEGORIES:kids\,Keene Public Library
DESCRIPTION:Calling all builders! Come build with LEGO® bricks\, we have 
 a huge variety of bricks to encourage your imagination to go wild. Our Bui
 ld-a-Rama club is open to kids of all ages.\nSource: Keene Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:98b03feb920b0ed1@kidcal
DTSTAMP:20260819T001543Z
DTSTART:20260929T220000Z
DTEND:20260929T230000Z
SUMMARY:Digital Resource Spotlight: Peterson's Test and Career Prep
LOCATION:Masiello Classroom
URL:https://keenenh.libcal.com/event/17178647
CATEGORIES:kids\,Keene Public Library
DESCRIPTION:Did you know your library card gives you free access to powerf
 ul online learning platforms\, skill-building tools\, and interactive data
 bases? Each month\, join us for a step-by-step demonstration of one of our
  featured digital resources. We’ll guide you through setting up an accou
 nt\, navigating the platform\, and making the most of its features for per
 sonal growth or career development. Bring your device to follow along\, or
  just sit back and watch!\n\nThis Month: Peterson's Test and Career Prep p
 repares you for upcoming standardized tests\, like the ACT\, SAT\, AP\, CL
 EP\, etc.\, and your college experience. It also offers in-depth informati
 on on undergraduate and graduate programs\, tuition and scholarship assist
 ance\, and more. Studying for U.S. Citizenship or preparing for the Firefi
 ghter exam? This digital resource has you covered. Plus\, it provides temp
 lates for creating resumés and cover letters.\nSource: Keene Public Libra
 ry
END:VEVENT
