SUMMARY:Paint N Sip
LOCATION:The Apiary\, 84 Pleasant Street\, Claremont\, 03743
URL:https://vermontjournal.com/event/paint-n-sip-2/
CATEGORIES:kids\,Vermont Journal & Shopper
DESCRIPTION:CLAREMONT\, N.H. – The Apiary\, 84 Pleasant Street in Clarem
 ont\, N.H.\, will host a guided watercolor painted experience led by artis
 t Tabitha Randall to create your own sea shells on Wednesday\, Aug. 19\, f
 rom 6-7:30 p.m. BYOB\, beverages\, and snacks.\nSource: Vermont Journal & 
 Shopper
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:9774a7fdd0a0e244@kidcal
DTSTAMP:20260819T001543Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260820T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260820T190000
SUMMARY:GMALL Presents Ada: My Mother the Architect
LOCATION:Manchester Community Library\, 138 Cemetery Avenue\, Manchester\,
  05255
URL:https://vermontjournal.com/event/gmall-presents-ada-my-mother-the-arch
 itect/
CATEGORIES:kids\,Vermont Journal & Shopper
DESCRIPTION:Green Mountain Academy is excited to present the documentary f
 ilm screening of Ada: My Mother the Architect. Ada Karmi Melamede is one o
 f the most accomplished architects in the world\, but very little is known
  about her outside of her home country of Israel. The movie is a deeply mo
 ving portrait of an extraordinary woman directed by her daughter\, filmmak
 er and former architect. It profiles a woman and artist deeply tested by t
 he realities of career and motherhood\, and a unique mother-daughter bond.
  Despite personal sacrifices\, Ada’s work gave physical form to some of 
 Israel’s highest democratic ideals\, most notably in the Supreme Court B
 uilding in Jerusalem\, the Open University\, Ben Gurion Airport\, and nume
 rous civic institutions around the country. A talk back with producer/dire
 ctor Yael Melamede will follow the screening. For more information or to p
 urchase tickets\, please call our office at 802-867-0111 or visit www.gree
 nmtnacademy.org.\nSource: Vermont Journal & Shopper
END:VEVENT
